
Arch New Installer live environment.

To begin the guided installation, type:

    install-arch

To repair an existing installation, replace @ from a Snapper snapshot,
or reinstall the OS preserving selected state, type:

    rescue-root

The installer checks internet access first. If offline, connect using iwctl:

  1. Run: iwctl
  2. Run: device list
     Replace wlan0 below with your wireless device.
  3. Run: station wlan0 scan
  4. Run: station wlan0 get-networks
  5. Run: station wlan0 connect "Your Wi-Fi name"
     Enter the Wi-Fi password when prompted.
  6. Run: exit (to leave iwctl)
  7. Wait a few seconds, then run install-arch or rescue-root again.
